input.body:
The owner is weighing turning Claudinite from a public repo into a commercial product bought through the GitHub app market, with a free single-repo tier and a paid fleet/organisation tier (Shepherd-style growth across many repos, plus user management, approvals and per-user differentiation).

This issue tracks the **research write-up only** — no decision, no plan. Deliverable: a document in `docs/` that presents

- what the product technically *is* today (vendored plaintext corpus, customer-side compute, no server, no accounts) and which of those properties a paid model breaks;
- the distribution/licensing options, each costed against the current feature set;
- what GitHub Marketplace actually permits (paid listings need a GitHub App owned by a verified-publisher org, Actions are not sellable, per-unit means per-user, the free-plan restriction);
- pricing-model options and which technical enforcement each one implies;
- what an organisational Shepherd (enterprise adoption) needs beyond today's single-PAT, single-fleet design.

Business-model and technical-path decisions stay with the owner; the document presents options with effort ranges, it does not choose.

Search-verified facts are cited inline in the document; anything unverifiable from this session is marked as such.

